Package: nitRo
Title: Find and Fix Slow or Unsafe Patterns in R Code
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Vishal Kumar", "Sharma", , "vishalsharma3003@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Analyses R code for common performance problems and unsafe
    idioms without running it, using a registry of pattern-matching rules
    that cover base R, vector allocation, loops, 'dplyr', 'data.table',
    file input and output, string handling, arithmetic and parallel
    processing. Rules whose rewrite gives identical results, such as
    replacing apply(m, 1, sum) with rowSums(m), are applied automatically.
    The original and rewritten code can then be run side by side to check
    that their results are identical and to compare their speed with
    'microbenchmark'.
